PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority consensus (10/13 colleagues) strongly favors B: add TSO immediately after UMI on existing poly(dT) bead oligo to enable template-switching/5'-RACE-style capture during RT. This places CDR3 (far upstream in TCR V(D)J) directly adjacent to cell-label/UMI, so the fixed 75×225 run covers it without altering bead chemistry, workflow, or sequencing cost. Core evidence: standard 3'-poly(dT) capture + 225 bp Read 2 only reaches constant-region/J, missing CDR3 by hundreds of nt. 

Minority views: C (2 colleagues) proposes bead redesign with flanking TCR capture oligos (directly enriches CDR3 but requires new surface chemistry incompatible with validated AbSeq/Sample-Tag workflow); A (1) adds TCR-specific oligos to beads (still 3'-biased, distance problem unsolved). D and E rejected by all as they either assume CDR3 already captured or violate cost/sequencing constraint.

Unresolved: exact timing of TSO addition (bead oligo vs. post-RT) and BD Rhapsody protocol compatibility details, but principle of 5'-tagging is consistent with commercial immune-repertoire kits. No errors noted in majority reasoning. My prior knowledge aligns with B; no belief change.}

