PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Consensus stable at 12/15 for B. Core problem unchanged: poly(dT)-only beads + 75×225 sequencing is strictly 3′-biased; CDR3 lies hundreds of nt upstream and is never captured. B satisfies every explicit constraint (identical bead schematic/UMI/cell-label, retained AbSeq/Sample-Tag/mRNA panels, BD Rhapsody workflow, 75×225 modality) by inserting TSO after UMI, enabling 5′-RACE/template switching so the same Read 2 covers V(D)J. Matches documented BD immune-repertoire 5′ protocols on identical beads. 

Minority C votes (7/13/14) correctly flag empirical risk: TSO efficiency unvalidated in dense multiplex AbSeq/Sample-Tag context on the same bead surface; could affect yield or introduce nonspecific products. They prefer C as lower-risk surface-composition adjustment without new enzymatic steps. However, any TCR-flanking capture oligos on beads constitutes non-trivial redesign explicitly disallowed by “keep the same bead schematic” and risks disrupting already-optimized multi-omic assays. A/D retain 3′-bias; E violates cost constraint. 

No factual errors; disagreement is risk tolerance vs. boundary conditions. Unresolved: real-world TSO performance under this exact multiplex load (downstream optimization question, not fundamental incompatibility). B remains the only minimal, protocol-validated solution meeting all stated constraints. Prior rounds’ reasoning on distance problem and bead redesign prohibition preserved.}

